PS: in the Nimble code I separate the variates into two groups: the two real ones, whose data are contained in Rdata (5 points × 2 variates); and the two categorical ones, whose data are contained in Cdata (5 points × 2 variates). In principle I could have used just one object with indexing 1:2 for the real and 3:4 for the categorical; but the solution above is a little more convenient.

With includecat=FALSE, all the categorical data and components are excluded. The problem reduces to 5 points of two real variates. In this case the getSamplesDPmeasure() works without problems.

Hope this clarifies things a little!

