> > Hi Suzy,
> >
> > I hope this email  finds you well!
> >
> > The differences in the cluster assignment that you are observing when using the dnorm_vec4 function are because you are not fixing the seed in the mcmc. If you add the argument setSeed = TRUE to nimbleMCMC() you should get the same results.
> >
> > Also, when looking into the mcmc’s output, don’t look only at the cluster labels. Look also at the parameters of the clusters. You can get two different labels in two different mcmc runs and probably the cluster parameters of those clusters are going to be very similar in the two runs.
> >
> > From your simulation of the data, the columns are all the same. And if I understood your code correctly, you are clustering columns.  So, it is not surprising that you get all your N-dimensional (column) observations clustered into a single cluster.
> >
> > I hope this helps and if you have any questions or something is not clear enough, please let me know.
> >
> > Best,
> > Claudia
